(Abstract) Tj
T*
(While biologic medications improve inflammation markers in inflammatory bowel disease,) Tj
T*
(symptom burden from pain and fatigue often persists. We randomized 780 participants \(mean) Tj
T*
(age 43 years, 58% female\) to receive digital self-management support \(n=391\) or standard) Tj
T*
(outpatient care \(n=389\) over 12 months. Primary disease-specific quality-of-life measures) Tj
T*
(showed modest improvements in both arms, with between-group differences not reaching) Tj
T*
(statistical significance for the pre-specified primary endpoint. However, secondary) Tj
T*
(analyses revealed consistent trends favoring the intervention across symptom domains. The) Tj
T*
(digital-intervention group accumulated 0.016 additional quality-adjusted life years \(95%) Tj
T*
(CI 0.002-0.030\). Health system costs were г304.66 lower \(95% CI -г803.51 to г194.18\) in) Tj
T*
(the intervention arm, driven primarily by reduced outpatient visit frequency. Cost-) Tj
T*
(effectiveness analysis indicated the intervention yielded cost savings of approximately) Tj
T*
(г28,633 per additional quality-adjusted life year gained from the healthcare perspective.) Tj
T*
(Results suggest digital symptom-focused self-management offers economic benefits) Tj
T*
(regardless of primary endpoint achievement.) Tj
